<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If4cc44daa8beb24d6afe83ca773174ec840a7da9" commit="ab470b46cd63272bf501cbee4f31ca70c5b06edc" commit_message="crash: modernize code with C++11 range-based for loop  Using C++11 range-based for loop in many cases improves readability and makes code less error-prone by avoiding the need for using a loop index or iterator, and explicitly specifying the container size or end for loop termination.  Also fixed some declarations of string array constants to conform to const-correctness and the naming convention suggested by the style guide.  BUG=None TEST=Run unit tests.  Change-Id: If4cc44daa8beb24d6afe83ca773174ec840a7da9 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/416375 Commit-Ready: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="416375" owner_email="benchan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/75/416375/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8dba2508c6c37b17ccfb9b5dd97481ba3f79e301" commit="4098f030d7519fca5b976552fcbda40417ae09da" commit_message="deqp: Add android-cts-7.0_r3 version for Android N  This adds deqp support for Android N. Note that it is still masked, if you want to try it you need to unmask it.  BUG=none TEST=builds  Change-Id: I8dba2508c6c37b17ccfb9b5dd97481ba3f79e301 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/416312 Commit-Ready: Ilja H. Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ilja H. Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ilja H. Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="416312" owner_email="marcheu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/12/416312/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If95b78d2a74ed3645c6b10d0ea737b0af2653401" commit="ed2320e93c2175ee6f91b74a5c8ca85dd0e29181" commit_message="power: Log a few more cases when the idle action is ignored.  Make powerd log an informative message when the default idle action is ignored due to the disable_idle_suspend pref being set (as happens automatically in dev/test images) or an update being applied while on AC power.  These overrides happen when powerd is computing its settings, so while it was possible to see that the Chrome-supplied action was being ignored in the current logs, the reason why was non-obvious.  BUG=chromium:666430 TEST=manual: used set_power_policy to set a 1m idle delay,      then watched the logs and saw &quot;Not performing idle      action because disable_idle_suspend powerd pref is set      (done automatically in dev)&quot;  Change-Id: If95b78d2a74ed3645c6b10d0ea737b0af2653401 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/416374 Commit-Ready: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Toni Barzic &lt;tbarzic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="416374" owner_email="derat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/74/416374/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I96398b2e4419d0f84b6dfb38f0f36bb9515bd2be" commit="7adac0b1e2510a9a9ab118f149e10e4d77332ebd" commit_message="login: Add use flag switch for kiosk mode migration  Allows us to easily turn on and off the changes associated with making rialto run in standard kiosk mode with attestation-based enterprise enrollment.  BUG=chromium:669287 TEST=Deploy to test device both with and without the use flag, and verify that it has the intended effect.  Change-Id: I96398b2e4419d0f84b6dfb38f0f36bb9515bd2be Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/414613 Commit-Ready: Niranjan Kumar &lt;kumarniranjan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Niranjan Kumar &lt;kumarniranjan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Jonathan Dixon &lt;joth@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="414613" owner_email="kumarniranjan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/13/414613/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I524ba356993fb2eee9bdd54592bb4650f571b88b" commit="cc5c3806d08f24b4fba647eff2d8a04554f74410" commit_message="UPSTREAM: net: phy: Make sure phy_start() always re-enables the phy interrupts  This is an alternative way of fixing:  commit db9683fb412d (&quot;net: phy: Make sure PHY_RESUMING state change                       is always processed&quot;)  When the PHY state transitions from PHY_HALTED to PHY_RESUMING, there are two things we need to do: 1). Re-enable interrupts (and power up the physical link, if powered down) 2). Update the PHY state and net-device based on the link status.  There's no strict reason why #1 has to be done from within the main phy_state_machine() function. There is a risk that other changes to the PHY (e.g. setting speed/duplex, which calls phy_start_aneg()) could cause a subsequent state transition before phy_state_machine() has processed the PHY_RESUMING state change. This would leave the PHY with interrupts disabled and/or still in the BMCR_PDOWN/low-power mode.  Moving enabling the interrupts and phy_resume() into phy_start() will guarantee this work always gets done. As the PHY is already in the HALTED state and interrupts are disabled, it shouldn't conflict with any work being done in phy_state_machine(). The downside of this change is that if the PHY_RESUMING state is ever entered from anywhere else, it'll also have to repeat this work.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:58374 TEST=emerge-gale gale-kernel-3_18 ap-configure --wan_connection_type=bridged/dhcp ethtool wan0 Change-Id: I524ba356993fb2eee9bdd54592bb4650f571b88b Signed-off-by: Tim Beale &lt;tim.beale@alliedtelesis.co.nz&gt; Signed-off-by: David S. Miller &lt;davem@davemloft.net&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/406501 Commit-Ready: Yuji Sasaki &lt;sasakiy@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Yuji Sasaki &lt;sasakiy@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Yuji Sasaki &lt;sasakiy@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="406501" owner_email="sasakiy@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/01/406501/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="9043.0.0-rc4"/></manifest>